From c8857d6b8f3d3d4e7f6b038b1a861d6ccaff08e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:49:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] (b) v2, part b-3: usrguide: float and classic hyperref

Round-4 finding R4-L2 (R4V-F2): "With float the kernel definition is
used" came right after the sentence that names hyperref without
\DocumentMetadata as an exception, but could be read as covering float
with that hyperref as well. It does not: hyperref replaces \caption
after the first aid for float, so \caption* still gives "Figure 2: *".
The sentence now says "without hyperref, or with \DocumentMetadata".
---
 base/doc/usrguide.tex | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/doc/usrguide.tex b/base/doc/usrguide.tex
index 8517766ed..39c27e416 100644
--- a/base/doc/usrguide.tex
+++ b/base/doc/usrguide.tex
@@ -1555,8 +1555,9 @@ and classes that replace \cs{caption} itself (at present, for example,
 \pkg{beamer}, and some journal and thesis classes) do not know
 \cs{caption*} yet: with them \verb|\caption*{Text}| gives, as before, a
 numbered caption with the text `*' and a list entry, followed by `Text'.
-With \pkg{float} the kernel definition is used (also for floats restyled
-by \pkg{float}, which show only their last caption). The \pkg{captcont}
+With \pkg{float} (without \pkg{hyperref}, or with \cs{DocumentMetadata})
+the kernel definition is used, also for floats restyled by \pkg{float},
+which show only their last caption. The \pkg{captcont}
 package has a \cs{caption*} of its own, which gives a numbered caption
 without list entry. The \pkg{caption} package supports \cs{caption*}
 with \pkg{hyperref}, \pkg{beamer} and \pkg{float}, but not with every
